  "coverage_explanation": "Tests the default potentiometer display at zero, intermediate values, and full scale; button override to 8888; persistence of the override while the potentiometer changes; release restoring the current potentiometer reading; and a repeated press/release cycle. Authoritative remapping places the potentiometer on A1, not the original A0.",
  "assumptions": [
    "The authoritative hardware assignments are A1 for the potentiometer, D2 for the button, and D4/D5 for TM1637 CLK/DIO.",
    "Rely on the disclosed button bench default: the button connects D2 to GND, uses INPUT_PULLUP, and is pressed at physical LOW.",
    "Interpret the unscaled potentiometer value as its raw ADC reading, 0 through 1023; no voltage conversion or alternate scale is specified.",
    "The button override applies while the button is held; releasing it restores the default potentiometer display.",
    "Leading blanks or zeros are permitted because no display padding format is specified."
  ],
